/-! # Real-time shift invariance of the area mixture on the càdlàg coding

`Process/AreaClockRealTimeShift` proves that the area-weighted two-sided law
`𝕢 = ∑_v a_v ℙ^v` of the area clock has shift-invariant finite-dimensional distributions at
arbitrary real times.  `Temporal/FixedEnvironmentTemporalTransport` consumes shift invariance
of the corresponding mixture on the càdlàg coding `CadlagPath S`
(`IsShiftInvariantMixture`).  This file is the bridge: **any** family of coded laws with the
finite-dimensional distributions of the two-sided process (`CodedTwoSidedLaw`) has a
shift-invariant area mixture — the manuscript's

> The sigma-finite path measure `𝕢_H = ∑_v a_v ℙ_H^v` is invariant under every
> deterministic time shift.  This follows directly from the Markov cylinder distributions
> and `a_v p_t(v,u) = a_u p_t(u,v)`.

The route is `CadlagPath.measurePreserving_timeShift_of_ratEval_law` (the coding σ-algebra
is generated by rational times), with the two σ-finite laws on `ℚ → S` identified by
`Measure.ext_of_generateFrom_of_iUnion` on the π-system of point cylinders
(`S` countable; the cover is by `{ξ 0 = c}`, of mass at most one cell area).

## Hypotheses

* `IsReflectedWalk` and detailed balance at every time (discharged for the area clock by
  `AreaReversibility.processTransitionReversible_cellArea`);
* an injective coding `code : Option V → S` (the manuscript's `ℕ ∪ {∞}` with every
  nonvertex state collapsed to `∞`), `S` countable;
* `CodedTwoSidedLaw PF code P`: `P v` has the finite-dimensional distributions of the coded
  two-sided process from `v`.  **Satisfiable**: it holds whenever `P v` is the image of
  `twoSidedStartLaw PF v` under an a.s. defined coding map into `CadlagPath S`
  (`codedTwoSidedLaw_of_map`); no such map is constructed for the actual process in the tree.

## What is *not* proved

The existence of the coding map for the actual two-sided area-clock path (càdlàg in the
one-point compactification: right-regularity (ii)+(R) forward, left limits for the reversed
half from `Forms/VertexIndicatorLeftLimits`), hence of a `MarkedPathProcess` for the actual
process.  Nothing here certifies `ScaledRootChainSystem.transport` or either main theorem.
-/

