/-! # The fixed-environment half of `p:lem:timeMTP`, welded to the annealed half

`Temporal/ActualAnnealedTemporalTransport.actualTemporalMassTransport` proves the annealed step
of the manuscript proof of `p:lem:timeMTP` (tex:1379-1397) for a `MarkedPathProcess`:

```
  E ∑_{H'} E_H^{H_0} ∫ 1_{X_t = H'} V(Ω,0,t) dt  =  E ∑_v (a_v/a_o) E_H^v ∫ 1_{X_t = o} V(Ω,0,t) dt,
```

and names the remaining producer: "for each deterministic `t`, shift the sigma-finite measure
`𝕢_H = ∑_v a_v ℙ_H^v` by `t`" — the **fixed-environment half**.  This file supplies it and
assembles the two halves into the manuscript's identity `p:eq:timeMTP` itself,

```
  E ∫_ℝ V(Ω,0,t) dt  =  E ∫_ℝ V(Ω,t,0) dt ,
```

for the marked process, with the fixed-environment shift invariance as the one named input.

## What is proved

* `sum_mul_lintegral_pathNumerator_eq` — **the fixed-environment half**, on the càdlàg
  coding, for any countable family of laws `P v` mixed with any weights `a v`:
  if `𝕢 = ∑_v a_v P v` is invariant under every real time shift and `P v` starts at
  `label v`, then for every measurable time-shift covariant `W`,
  `∑_v a_v E^v ∫ 1_{X_t = label o} W(0,t) dt = a_o E^o ∫ W(s,0) ds`.
  Route: `TemporalMassTransport.lintegral_lintegral_timeTransport` applied to the
  root-marked kernel `W'(ω,s,t) = 1_{ω_t = label o} W(ω,s,t)`, which is again covariant.
* `rootedIncoming_eq_of_fixedEnvironment`, `rootedOutgoing_eq_of_target` — the two
  expressions of `actualTemporalMassTransport`, identified with `E^{H_0} ∫ V(s,0) ds` and
  `E^{H_0} ∫ V(0,t) dt`.  The cell-area factor cancels by `cellVolume_pos_lt_top`.
* `lintegral_timeMTP_of_fixedEnvironment` — **`p:eq:timeMTP` for the marked process**,
  from `MassTransport ν` and, for `ν`-a.e. environment, `FixedEnvironmentShiftInvariant`
  (the σ-finite area mixture is real-time shift invariant, and `ℙ_H^v` starts at `v`),
  time-shift covariance of `V`, and "values at nonvertex target times are set to zero".
* `isShiftInvariantMixture_const` — **satisfiability** of the shift hypothesis in the
  abstract form (constant-path laws).

## Why the root is the Palm root (the handoff's trap)

The shift invariance is of the **area-weighted σ-finite mixture** `∑_v a_v ℙ_H^v`, never of
a single `ℙ_H^v`; the passage to one root happens only after spatial mass transport, at the
root cell `H_0` of the environment law.  The identity is false for a fixed environment and a
single start (`outputs/fable-regenerative-invariance-handoff.md`, TRAP), and nothing here
asserts it there.

## What is *not* proved

The hypothesis `FixedEnvironmentShiftInvariant` for the **actual** marked process.  Its
finite-dimensional content — real-time shift invariance of `∑_v a_v ℙ_H^v` on every finite
set of real times — is `Process/AreaClockRealTimeShift.twoSidedSpeedLaw_cellArea_realCyl_shift`
(unconditional); the transfer to the coding is `Temporal/AreaClockCodingShift`.  No
`MarkedPathProcess` for the actual process is constructed anywhere.  Nothing here certifies
`ScaledRootChainSystem.transport` (`ParabolicTemporalTransport` on the rooted flow), the
marked `p:lem:timeMTP`, or either main theorem.
-/

